Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: re-read VBUS when leaving the sink role

0061 limits the vSafe0V VBUS fallback to the sink role and clears that state
in start_toggling(). The last VBUS reading TCPM got may still have come from
the fallback ("VBUS on" while sinking), and no interrupt fires when the
supply later discharges to vSafe0V, so TCPM kept vbus_present and never
attached as source (SRC_ATTACH_WAIT) to the next, unpowered partner. Signal
a VBUS change after clearing the sink state so TCPM re-reads it.
Nura-Category: local-workaround
Nura-Origin: nura rc4h dock debugging
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2
---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-11-13 21:07:03.507850969 +0100
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/qcom/qcom_pmic_typec_port.c	2026-11-13 21:07:36.214313188 +0100
@@ -606,6 +606,7 @@
 	unsigned int misc;
 	u8 mode = 0;
 	unsigned long flags;
+	bool was_sinking = false;
 	int ret;
 
 	switch (port_type) {
@@ -631,6 +632,7 @@
 		misc, !!(misc & CC_ATTACHED), port_type, pmic_typec_port->cc, cc);
 
 	qcom_pmic_set_cc_debounce(pmic_typec_port);
+	was_sinking = READ_ONCE(pmic_typec_port->sinking);
 	WRITE_ONCE(pmic_typec_port->sinking, false);
 
 	/* force it to toggle at least once */
@@ -646,6 +648,15 @@
 done:
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&pmic_typec_port->lock, flags);
 
+	/*
+	 * The last VBUS reading may have used the sink-only vSafe0V fallback.
+	 * No interrupt fires when a discharging supply finally reaches
+	 * vSafe0V, so make TCPM re-read VBUS now that the fallback is off;
+	 * otherwise it never sees vSafe0V and stays in SRC_ATTACH_WAIT.
+	 */
+	if (was_sinking)
+		tcpm_vbus_change(pmic_typec_port->tcpm_port);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
